Z||000010||Devotshka||11-22-2001||07:31 PM||||A good friend of mine had a Jimmy with the 4.3L engine in it, and from day one he got between 12-15mpg, a few 17mpg peaks, and on the highway around 22 or so.  He never shut up about how horrible it was on gas.  If you are so concerned about gas mileage, buy a Geo, a 4.3L is not going to put you in any better place than a fieros MPG by a long shot.  <BR>I will note that in that truck it did cruise quite nicely, however.<BR>... and btw, my vote would go for the black one.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Galen||11-22-2001||07:51 PM||||Not to defend sweet or anything, but you ppl need to calm down and get ya head out ya a$$. I personally like the black one.. a lil big for me but it still looks nice.<P>Spektrum, you dont come here for respect do you? Sure I've 'dis'sed ( <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">) ricers before, but sheesh, act like a dumba$$ why dont ya. A truck that has 4 wheels, two doors(or four), an engine, a transmission and requires gas(or diesel) is no differant than anyone elses car or SUV. Its a vehicle to get you from point a to point b. Who really gives a shiznit if anyone likes it or not? Spek, go look in a mirror, that person looking back at you needs to grow up.<P>------------------<BR><B><FONT COLOR="purple">Ray</FONT></B> - <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank>Fierolinks</A>||||reg||1
Z||000012||Mach10||11-22-2001||07:54 PM||||*smacks Galen for misuse of word "Shiznit"*<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I agree with most else. Even though I can't STAND low-rider trucks (especially the ones that say "Z-71 Offroad" on them  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>But whatever turns your crank...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I just think that you'd be DOWNGRADING from a Fiero  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
