Z||000014||broys||11-22-2001||08:11 PM||||My '96 blazer 4x4 has the 4.3 and it only gets 18 mpg in mixed driving. But that's when I'm driving like a grandma. If I hotrod it just even a little bit then it jumps down to 16. <P>Someone I know used to have an 89 Chevy truck similar to what you want. It had the v8 though. Very fast for a truck.||||reg||1
Z||000015||Standard||11-22-2001||08:21 PM||||You can't afford the gas, but you can afford a tricked out truck...?  Save yourself a couple thousand and get an early 90's honda or something if you're so concerned about gas mileage.  Like the others have said, A 4.3 isn't gonna be too much easier on gas than a 5.7... Add that to the fact that it's in a <B>truck</B>... Not really the economy type of vehicle.  <P>Now say it with me..<BR>"think before purchase"||||reg||1
Z||000016||loafer87gt||11-22-2001||08:34 PM||||The 4.3 is a total gas hog. My landlords have one in their blazer and the highest milege they have gotten is 17 highway. One of my friends has a newer 328 Chev  truck and that thing gets mid twenties. Go v8, the lower revs on the highway will make up for the extra 2 cylinders. ||||reg||1
Z||000017||Nashco||11-22-2001||08:35 PM||||yo_sweet, don't think in mileage in terms of, "bigger engine uses more fuel," rather, "the more you push that pedal on the right, the more fuel you use."<P>A truck with a 4.3 is underpowered, and as a result, you will constantly be on the throttle.  This not only uses a lot of fuel, but also abuses the engine more than necessary.  Also, I thought the 4.3 only came with a 5 speed (correct me if I'm wrong)...and 5 speeds suck in daily driver trucks.<P>With a 350, you have a lot more power to draw from, so you don't need to be using so much throttle all the time to accomplish the same performance.  This makes it so you use about the same or LESS fuel than the 4.3 in normal driving, but if you *need* more power, it's there.<P>I like the black truck, by the way.  I've actually always wanted to get a 1st gen S10 truck with a 4.3.  They are getting really cheap nowadays, and look pretty good lowered with nice rims on them.  Oh, and they're SO easy to work on it's almost disgusting.  Parts are cheap, aftermarket parts aplenty, and I still get to have a 2 seater with power (except there's TRUNK SPACE! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">).  Oh, and contrary to popular belief, some trucks don't handle like sh!t.  I drove a stock 94 Ranger, that drove like crap.  An S10 lowered a couple inches on good rubber handles just as good as most cars, though.  They're light, lots of weight, and as long as you don't rely on the rear end of the truck too much, you're fine.<P>My 2 cents...<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000018||4UMLA1||11-22-2001||08:36 PM||||I hate to tell you my friend, you are crazy as hell to give up a Fiero for one of those!||||reg||13
Z||000019||Black86SE||11-22-2001||08:50 PM||||My grandpa has the 4.3 in his '90 tahoe, and that truck has no guts. My bicycle has more get up than that. I have a '93 Silverado 4x4 with the 350 and oversized tires. I get around 13-15 mpg. And I do step on it (my driving record shows that). I have had it since I was about 17, maybe 16. I am 20 now and I can say that gas isn't really a problem. I worked part time up until I graduated in '99 and I really didn't have a problem with gas. Yeah I had to borrow money for gas from my parents once in a while but that was due to me spending money on things I didn't need. Now I work 31 hours a week (had to cut back due to college) and I drive about an hour each way to visit my girlfriend at another college almost once a week. The gas is only a problem when it hits $2/gallon and I am empty. But I usually fill up the tank when I get gas. If you have any questions about those trucks let me know. I love mine and would only sell it for a newer one. FYI, I noticed that the new S-10 ZR-2's only get 14 mpg city with the Vortec 4300. <P>This is a link to the site that has pics of my truck and my trips to the sand dunes. CAUTION: Web page loads slow (even on 56k). Many pics and big ones at that. <p>[This message has been edited by Black86SE (edited 11-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000020||yo_sweet||11-22-2001||08:50 PM||||my first intent was to go for a 3rd gen Trans Am but my dad says it will kill me on gas!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> , then he told me to pick up one of those short boxes after i sell my car i could go 350 or 4.3l but i firged v6 isint so bad on gas , its not really that big of a deal but i like the milage i get out of my fiero also the insurance is said to be cheaper i pay $250 per month for my fiero<BR>and it will be a cold day in hell when i buy a rice buket!||||reg||1
Z||000021||Spektrum-87GT||11-22-2001||09:01 PM||||i didnt mean to bash trucks, just pimped out trucks because it doesnt make any sense... PERIOD! that coupled with the fact he's worrying about gas milage when the truck itself is going to cost a LOT and its going to cost a lot to modify like that.<P>keep the fiero!!! i'd never thought i'd say this, but its more practical!!! decent gas milage, good performance, and you can even pimp it out if you want for a lot less money.<P>advantages of the truck over a fiero?<BR>none, if you dont want to haul anything.<P>advantages of a fiero over a truck?<BR>too long to list, but i'll say price and fun factor||||reg||1
Z||000022||Nashco||11-22-2001||09:24 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Spektrum-87GT:<BR><B>i didnt mean to bash trucks, just pimped out trucks because it doesnt make any sense... PERIOD! that coupled with the fact he's worrying about gas milage when the truck itself is going to cost a LOT and its going to cost a lot to modify like that.<P>keep the fiero!!! i'd never thought i'd say this, but its more practical!!! decent gas milage, good performance, and you can even pimp it out if you want for a lot less money.<P>advantages of the truck over a fiero?<BR>none, if you dont want to haul anything.<P>advantages of a fiero over a truck?<BR>too long to list, but i'll say price and fun factor</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Spek, open your mind buddy, other people like different things than you, if you could imagine such a thing!  How about if you want to swap in a big block.  How well can you do that with a Fiero?  Not nearly as easy as it is to do with a truck.  What about off-roading, how well does a fiero do that compared to a truck?  What if the owner wants 10 12" subs and the amps to power it, all the while still having room for his girlfriend to ride along?  Have you ever gone for a ride in a FAST truck?  Have you ever rode in a truck that was lowered properly?<P>Yes, you DID mean to bash trucks, and that's exactly what you're doing.  I've never owned a truck, and will never own a full size truck.  Regardless, I have enough sense to know there are a lot of reasons a person could want a truck.  There are even more reasons a person could want to "pimp out" a truck.  Again...open your mind, it's closed way too tight.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000023||87fastback||11-22-2001||10:30 PM||||I have to agree with Nashco on the fuel mileage issue.  Just because you have a smaller engine does NOT mean you will get better gas mileage.  He is right that the smaller engine has to work twice as hard to keep the extra weight of that truck up to speed.<P>I have worked for GM for a number of years and the best you will EVER see out of a GM truck (even the S10 Blazers w/4.3's) is going to be 18-22mpg.  Any other figure those people are lying to themselves.  I have owned them all and you will NEVER see the mileage you get out of a daily driver Fiero.<P>It looks like that is your primary concern, so in that case I would reconsider.  Lowered trucks look cool and all, but it really does defeat the purpose.  But to each his own!||||reg||1
Z||000024||artherd||11-22-2001||10:38 PM||||The black one looks ok, I like the American Racing Torque Thrust wheels on it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> (I really like those wheels on almost any older car. Haden't thought of them on a truck yet.)<P>I agree with previously posted, you can afford a PIMPED OUT PICKUP but not some bloody gas?  <P>You're getting the wrong thing if you want to save gas man.<P>Besides, trucks are for working (hauling big ugly stuff.) Fieros are for *driving*  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I just sold my Ferrari to buy a friggin escelade. Aren't I cool?  No, I'm not. Sorry.<P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000025||FieroKyle||11-23-2001||12:11 AM||||I love the top one. Definetly. The 4.3L is slow but pretty good on gas. My Dad has a w/t 94 Chevy with it. Definetly gets great milage, upper twenties, but thats with the manual and heavy duty clutch. I don't like the bottom one however.<P>Whats wrong with the top truck? Its not cheesy, has good rims, no stickers, definetly not ricey. I like the taste. I wouldn't get it over the Fiero, once you drive a sportscar you never go back.<P>Also they are not wanna be trucks. I'll tell you what I hate on trucks, when they are on stilts 12 feet in the air with straight pipes or a cherry bomb and are louder than hell. Has big ole mudding tires (for all that street pimping on red neck corner) and the kid driving it thinks he is a bad ass king of the road.<P>Again if anything he was suggesting opinions, you guys are ripping him a new a$$hole.<p>[This message has been edited by FieroKyle (edited 11-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000026||Pontiaddict||11-23-2001||07:43 AM||||If you're going to get a truck with a 4.3 in it, get a 92 or later with the Vortec motor in it. The earlier ones are worthless.<P>Of the two trucks you have pictured, I throw my vote in for the top one. It looks like it was done tastefully unlike the second one<P>I used to have an 86 Trans Am 305HO 5 speed. I got around 18mpg with it though I usually drove harder than I should. If you find a Firebird with 3.08 gears in it and fuel injection (mine had a bad carb and 3.42's) you should easily get past 20mpg. Or you could get a v6 car and save your money to swap in a 3.8. Which is what I'd do if I came across a good deal on a v6 'bird.||||reg||1
Z||000027||Fformula88||11-23-2001||10:08 AM||||If your a little short on cash, I am not sure a Chevy C/K is the way to go.  The 4.3L in one is gonna burn nearly as much gas as a V8 because it has to pull around all that weight.  Ever check out the EPA numbers of that engine in new S10's?  Its like 16-19 or something very close.  It would be worse in a full size.<P>If gas milage is your concern, a truck is not the way to go.  Maybe a 90's Grand Am GT with a 3.1L would be more your style.  Sporty looking, good V6 engine, and without the gas guzzling hulk of a truck to haul around.  Like has been said, a full size truck without a V8 just isn't much of a truck.  I don't think you'd be happy with a V6 in one.||||reg||1
Z||000028||Spektrum-87GT||11-23-2001||04:56 PM||||lol, i dont like to answer such flame bait, but i'll humor you. Swap a big block in a fiero? whats the point? you can fit a small block 350 in a fiero though... off roading in a lowered truck... hmm.. i think the fiero would be better off(i own a 91 cherokee and have been off roading though, its really fun). if you want 10 12" subs i feel bad for your ears and for your girlfriend. gone for a ride in a fast truck? anyone who wants to make a truck fast is not only stupid, but has way too much money and is way into image. If you want to go fast, get a sports car, NOT a truck. speed is fun no matter what kind of vehicle your in, but a sports car is more stable, costs less to go faster, etc. <P>listen, i OWN a truck, i'm not bashing them. Its great for hauling stuff... and... well thats about it. My mind isnt closed... i just reject stupidity. If you can give me a decent logical reason why, i'll listen, until then, stfu.<P>now turning them into off road beasts is a whole other story... its really cool as long as you take it off roading and dont pose! fake people suck!<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Nashco:<BR><B> <BR>Spek, open your mind buddy, other people like different things than you, if you could imagine such a thing!  How about if you want to swap in a big block.  How well can you do that with a Fiero?  Not nearly as easy as it is to do with a truck.  What about off-roading, how well does a fiero do that compared to a truck?  What if the owner wants 10 12" subs and the amps to power it, all the while still having room for his girlfriend to ride along?  Have you ever gone for a ride in a FAST truck?  Have you ever rode in a truck that was lowered properly?<P>Yes, you DID mean to bash trucks, and that's exactly what you're doing.  I've never owned a truck, and will never own a full size truck.  Regardless, I have enough sense to know there are a lot of reasons a person could want a truck.  There are even more reasons a person could want to "pimp out" a truck.  Again...open your mind, it's closed way too tight.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||6
Z||000029||lowCG||11-23-2001||06:59 PM||||Maybe with a supercharger,on the V8 model.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000030||thomas_l||11-24-2001||03:21 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Spektrum-87GT:<BR><B>what is the point of a pimped out truck(pimped out anything for that matter)? they're not original, they're not cool, they're not fast, they dont impress anyone besides the losers that own them(if you dont believe me, go to a real car show and you'll see a special 'lowriders and ricers' area where no one goes except people with lowriders and rice burners... and just take a look at the kind of people that own them)<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thank you for such special insight - I feel the love.<P>The 4.3L in a GM truck will get a tiny bit more mpg than the 8 cyl but not enough to bother IMHO. The 6 has to work harder to haul the weight and overcome the wind. I have an 02 Silverado with the 5.3L. It gets 12-14 mpg around town, best hwy was 19 mpg. Get what you want appearance-wise. I don't like a lot of things but appreciate hard work and creativity when I see it versus making a blanket statement that all owners are lusers. Some folks are just jealous and can't find the words to admit it without offending   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by thomas_l (edited 11-24-2001).]||||reg||1
