Z||000033||artherd||11-24-2001||08:19 PM||||Scarriest thing I've ever seen in my life:<P>At the Sears Point dragestrip, a big honking new Dodge Ram 3500 Cummins Diesel pulls up.<P>He has a big Keg of beer in the back. (no joke!)<P>It's been lifted, with big huge tyres, and then it takes off...<P>And is throrugh the traps (after the unholy black and blue smoke mix clears, several minuites...) 12.5seconds later...<P>Turns out that 'keg' is a 55gallon Nitrous Oxide bottle, and he's running about a 600bhp shot ...<P>On a DIESEL!~!!<P>Best!<BR>Ben<BR><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000034||Nashco||11-24-2001||08:36 PM||||Ha! That would be awesome!  What's funny is that I never even considered it; deisel motors are gluttons for punishment.  I'm willing to bet that thing even lasts a fair while doing that!  Man that'd be fun to totally show up some schmoes in a Camaro or even some Corvettes with a Dodge truck <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Damn though..those trucks cost enough in the first place, but all that NOS!!!  What kind of tires was he running; was it a duallie or no?<P>Bryce<P>||||reg||1
